    {
      "type": "info",
      "title": "Using two adjectives together",
      "text": "Adjectives go in this order: size → style → colour + noun. She has long straight blonde hair. He has big brown eyes.\n\nthin or slim? fat or overweight?\nThin and slim are both the opposite of fat, but slim = thin in an attractive way. Fat is not very polite. It is more polite to say someone is (a bit) overweight.\n\nhandsome or beautiful?\nHandsome is used for men, beautiful is used for women, and good-looking and attractive are used for both men and women."
    },
